diff --git a/docs/data-transfers.md b/docs/data-transfers.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..4a6be93
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/data-transfers.md
@@ -0,0 +1,71 @@
+# Exporting and importing Fizzy data
+
+Admins can export a complete account from **Account Settings → Export your account**.
+Anyone can export their visible cards from **their own profile → Export your cards**.
+Exports run in the background. Fizzy emails the requester a private download link
+when the ZIP is ready. That link expires 24 hours after generation; expired
+archives are purged by the recurring export cleanup task. Links also stop working
+if the requester loses permission to download the export.
+
+A personal export contains published cards from accessible boards and the person's
+own drafts, including closed and postponed cards. It never includes private boards
+they cannot access or other people's drafts. Each `cards/<number>.json` includes
+the card's description, comments, people, steps, tags, and attachment paths.
+Original pictures and files are under `files/<blob-id>/<filename>`.
+
+## Restoring an account
+
+Sign in and open `/account/imports/new` (also linked from the account chooser).
+Upload an **account** export; a personal cards export is not an account backup.
+No existing account membership is required. The import runs in the background and
+emails the signed-in identity on success or failure, including the failure reason.
+
+Imports create a **new account** and leave the original untouched. The importer is
+its owner and has access to every restored board. Other people are matched by email
+address, creating identities only when necessary; existing identities and their
+credentials are never modified. Source owners become admins if someone else imports
+the account. Database IDs and storage keys are remapped, and mentions, embedded files,
+board access, and saved filters point to the new records. Search and storage totals
+are rebuilt before completion. Hosted deployments use the normal signup tenant
+provisioning and cancellation hooks.
+
+An unsuccessful restoration rolls back account records, newly created people,
+search records, and storage totals, and deletes files uploaded during the attempt.
+The submitted ZIP is purged after either outcome. Job retries do not create another
+account or repeat a completion notification.
+
+Public board keys and webhook signing secrets are regenerated. Webhooks start
+**disabled**, and historical notification bundles are marked delivered so importing
+an account does not replay old emails or outbound requests. Sign-in links, sessions,
+API tokens, passkeys, billing information, and other export/import archives are not
+transferred. External images and videos remain external links; Fizzy does not fetch
+arbitrary remote URLs during a transfer.
+
+## Storage and archive format
+
+Account archives have a versioned `manifest.json`, portable records in
+`records/<table>/<id>.json`, readable card JSON, and attached file bytes. The manifest
+contains record/file counts. Imports only accept known record types and check
+references, ZIP CRCs, file sizes, and file checksums (MD5 or SHA-256). Paths are never extracted to
+user-supplied filesystem locations. Truncated archives, unsafe paths, duplicate
+entries, unsupported compression/encryption, excessive expansion, and oversized
+JSON records are rejected.
+
+ZIP64 is supported. ZIP output and file restoration stream to S3 multipart uploads
+or local disk. Reading uses Active Storage range requests instead of downloading an
+entire archive; a test covers a ZIP64 directory beyond 600 GB. JSON entries are limited
+to 32 MiB and central-directory reads to 128 MiB, independently of file/archive size.
+
+The import form uses direct uploads. Archives larger than 100 MiB use S3 multipart
+uploads (or a streamed Disk PUT), avoiding S3's single-request size limit. S3 CORS
+must allow `PUT` from the Fizzy origin and **expose the `ETag` response header**.
+Use private buckets. Incomplete uploads are aborted when possible and abandoned
+identity-owned uploads are cleaned up after a week. Keep the browser open until the
+upload finishes; the subsequent import does not require the browser to stay open.
+
+Run the focused regression suite with:
+
+```sh
+script/test-data-transfer
+bin/rails test test/system/account_imports_test.rb
+```
